WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Four workers died at TSMC's Kaoshong Fab site, halting steelwork across Taiwan. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, Episode 30. After the Kaoshong halt, an edge microcontroller announcement, a memory supply warning from Dell, then power and foundry moves, a tear down on optical test, and the dates sitting ahead. The dead men were on Taiwan's semiconductor manufacturing's Fab-22 job in Nanzi District, inside the southern Taiwan science park. Taipei Times reports the Kaoshong

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.820
Houshung Fire Department took the call at 453 in the afternoon yesterday.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.580
After four people were injured and sent 10 vehicles and 22 people, a steel structure

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:41.460
failed during hoisting and installation.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:46.500
The Southern Taiwan Science Park Bureau's early read is that bolts on a connecting plate

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.120
of an outer steel frame on the third floor snapped, and the workers fell with the steel.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.380
Three were pronounced dead last night.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.500
The fourth, surname Huang, died in intensive care this morning.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:57.680
Everything.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.220
All four worked for a domestic contractor.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.240
The independent carries TSMC's statement that the company and the contractor stop the

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:10.460
related work on that site and stop the same kind of steel structure work at every TSMC

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.940
construction site in Taiwan until the investigation is done.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.320
The Bureau has labor inspectors on cause and liability.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:23.000
Fab-22 is the fab scheduled for two nanometer chips and anything more advanced than that.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:30.535
Synaptics has introduced a part it is calling an XMCU, the Astra SR200 series, announced

00:01:30.535 --> 00:01:32.895
rather than described as in customer's hands.

00:01:33.575 --> 00:01:38.735
Tech PowerUp's account of the launch says the point is multimodal edge AI that a normal

00:01:38.735 --> 00:01:41.295
microcontroller cannot keep an on-chip memory.

00:01:41.855 --> 00:01:47.495
The announced design puts heterogeneous AI compute next to custom DRAM in the package, and

00:01:47.495 --> 00:01:50.875
that DRAM is described as scaling into the hundreds of megabytes.

00:01:50.875 --> 00:01:56.475
The AI block is Synaptics Torque Engine plus the Coral NPU from Google Research.

00:01:56.975 --> 00:02:03.195
Synaptics says this is the first time an ARM Cortex M85 has been paired with a Cortex M52.

00:02:04.015 --> 00:02:11.795
EE times, from Synaptics Tech Day in San Jose on October 20, puts the family at up to 400 giga operations per second,

00:02:12.295 --> 00:02:18.955
and 256 megabytes of that custom DRAM, with vision, audio, and hardware-rooted security on the die.

00:02:18.955 --> 00:02:25.615
three pin compatible tiers are named SR 210 is 200 giga operations per second

00:02:25.615 --> 00:02:32.215
aimed at always-on voice and sensing SR 230 is 300 and adds vision display and

00:02:32.215 --> 00:02:39.275
optional audio SR 250 is 400 with two vision paths and two display paths the

00:02:39.275 --> 00:02:44.435
intended boxes are wearables battery sensors connected cameras streamers and

00:02:44.435 --> 00:02:50.915
industrial vision and voice gear. John Wile, who runs IoT and Edge AI processors at Synaptics,

00:02:51.315 --> 00:02:54.895
said the traction so far is strongest in electronics worn on the body.

00:02:55.953 --> 00:03:01.113
Socio next is pushing agentic AI out of front-end chip design and into physical design of large

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:07.333
advanced node system on chips, working with cadence. Semiconductor Digest reports the first target

00:03:07.333 --> 00:03:14.553
is physical design of a large 3nm SOC using cadence's InnoStack AI super agent, with a plan to

00:03:14.553 --> 00:03:17.153
spread that agent across more SOC projects.

00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:24.113
The plumbing socio-next names is retrieval-augmented generation, model context protocol support, custom

00:03:24.113 --> 00:03:29.493
AI skills, and agents aimed at floor planning, custom timing checks, and checklist automation

00:03:29.493 --> 00:03:30.513
still on the roadmap.

00:03:31.193 --> 00:03:36.033
President and Chief Operating Officer Hisato Yoshida said the company expects up to a five

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:39.513
times productivity gain from Cadence's agentic workflow.

00:03:39.513 --> 00:03:45.253
Kaden's Chin-Chi-Tang, senior vice president, described in O-stack as open enough that

00:03:45.253 --> 00:03:46.893
a customer can load its own methods.

00:03:48.071 --> 00:03:53.031
An NTT-Advise consortium is developing mass production technology for optical chiplets.

00:03:53.731 --> 00:03:55.131
Semi-conductor digest reports.

00:03:55.851 --> 00:03:57.651
The companies in the group do the development.

00:03:58.351 --> 00:04:00.491
NTT's role, as stated, is advisor.

00:04:01.291 --> 00:04:03.791
This is a development program, not a factory start.

00:04:03.791 --> 00:04:09.754
Amazon has pledged 16 billion euros of investment in Germany in 2027.

00:04:10.434 --> 00:04:15.654
Data Center Dynamics says that Pledge covers more data centers and AI infrastructure, high-speed

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.334
satellite internet, and logistics.

00:04:17.974 --> 00:04:22.594
It is a pledged year of spending, not a named campus that has been energized, and the

00:04:22.594 --> 00:04:24.494
euros are not split out to one site.

00:04:25.438 --> 00:04:30.478
Central Georgia Electric Membership Corporation plans a 50-megawatt deployment of home batteries.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:35.318
Utility Dive says the batteries are meant to cut system peaks and energy costs while

00:04:35.318 --> 00:04:38.398
hyper-scale data centers try to connect to that cooperative's grid.

00:04:38.998 --> 00:04:43.798
Those 50 megawatts are storage on the utility side, not IT load inside a hall.

00:04:44.837 --> 00:04:50.377
OVH Cloud told its annual earnings call it has 110 megawatts of data center capacity it

00:04:50.377 --> 00:04:52.097
can use to grow the customer base.

00:04:52.677 --> 00:04:58.237
Data Center Dynamics reports, that is capacity the operator says it can sell, not a new site

00:04:58.237 --> 00:04:58.997
breaking ground.

00:04:58.997 --> 00:05:04.511
1. Michael Dell told the Wall Street Journal the memory shortage gets worse next year because

00:05:04.511 --> 00:05:10.111
AI data center construction keeps taking DRAM and high bandwidth memory. Techpowerup puts

00:05:10.111 --> 00:05:15.871
Dell's undelivered AI server orders at about $95 billion, which Dell called the largest

00:05:15.871 --> 00:05:21.611
backlog the company has had, and says memory is the constraint, not orders. The accelerators

00:05:21.611 --> 00:05:26.251
in those servers want high bandwidth memory. The servers around them still want ordinary

00:05:26.251 --> 00:05:32.531
D-RAM. Dell is buying D-RAM only when final assembly is close, and is signing long-term supply

00:05:32.531 --> 00:05:38.131
deals. Tech PowerUp lines Dell's view up with Micron's chief executive, who said supply

00:05:38.131 --> 00:05:45.031
will be much tighter in 2027 and 2028 than this year, and with SK Heinex's chief executive,

00:05:45.431 --> 00:05:51.102
who expects the shortage to run through 2030. Micron is putting strategic money into

00:05:51.102 --> 00:05:55.982
the Indian Corporation so Indian can expand refining and high-purity materials work in

00:05:55.982 --> 00:06:01.302
Rome, New York, and restart domestic processing of critical minerals used in advanced chips.

00:06:02.002 --> 00:06:06.882
Semiconductor Digest ties the check to a planned micron announced in July to invest up to

00:06:06.882 --> 00:06:10.122
$3 billion in the U.S. semiconductor supply chain.

00:06:10.762 --> 00:06:14.582
A long-term supply agreement is how micron gets access to those minerals.

00:06:15.262 --> 00:06:20.302
Chief procurement officer Ben Tesson connected that access to Micron's technology roadmap

00:06:20.302 --> 00:06:24.202
and to depending less on refining capacity concentrated overseas.

00:06:24.842 --> 00:06:30.022
Micron also restated that its expected U.S. fab and technology spend rises to more than

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:33.002
$250 billion through 2035.

00:06:33.822 --> 00:06:38.822
Governor Kathy Hockle said the Clay Fab project is months ahead of schedule and called it

00:06:38.822 --> 00:06:41.582
the largest private investment in New York State history.

00:06:42.565 --> 00:06:47.625
Today's TSMC process item is three nanometer production at the second factory of Japan

00:06:47.625 --> 00:06:49.665
Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing.

00:06:49.665 --> 00:06:54.385
The Kumamoto Joint Venture, and it is a plan, not waifers moving.

00:06:54.945 --> 00:06:59.265
Electronics for you reports total equipment investment in that venture is expected to

00:06:59.265 --> 00:07:00.545
exceed $23 billion.

00:07:01.725 --> 00:07:07.165
TSMC's Japan account said output and spending would come in phases, following market demand,

00:07:07.625 --> 00:07:10.145
and only with Japanese government support in place.

00:07:10.725 --> 00:07:15.685
A separate August agreement with Sony semiconductor solutions created advanced vision semiconductor

00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:19.625
Dr. Manufacturing in Kumamoto for next-generation image sensors.

00:07:20.526 --> 00:07:26.186
Reuters reports as an exclusive, that bite dance, Alibaba, and Tencent have placed more

00:07:26.186 --> 00:07:29.046
than $35 billion of NVIDIA chip orders.

00:07:29.586 --> 00:07:33.046
Those are orders placed, not chips the story describes as delivered.

00:07:33.998 --> 00:07:39.798
Biggo Finance, citing the Alec, also reports today that Elon Musk first tried to buy plants

00:07:39.798 --> 00:07:45.438
from Intel, TSMC, and micron, was turned down and moved tariffab onto partnerships,

00:07:45.438 --> 00:07:52.638
with Intel contributing its 14A process and Musk capping TSMC at a subcontractor role at most.

00:07:53.298 --> 00:08:01.238
A ruling party lawmaker in South Korea has attacked a planned AI data center grid code and asked for an exemption for projects already underway.

00:08:01.738 --> 00:08:09.638
The Register reports tens of thousands of NVIDIA GPUs in Meta's Prometheus Supercluster are sitting idle, kept ready for a failure.

00:08:09.638 --> 00:08:15.738
data center dynamics reports shade forms flex VMs turned bare metal GPU clusters into single

00:08:15.738 --> 00:08:20.758
tenant virtual machines on its marketplace and that an approved node can be enrolled in about

00:08:20.758 --> 00:08:27.078
30 minutes. Digitimes reports control and FSE are combining laser and plasma processes for

00:08:27.078 --> 00:08:33.958
advanced packaging. Pulse 2.0 reports Apple is expanding a $600 billion US manufacturing plan

00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:39.678
with CUNITY, Perryman, Broadcom, Corning, Coherent, TSMC, and AMCORE.

00:08:40.593 --> 00:08:45.093
Co-packaged optics stalls in the factory when the fiber array has to find the die without

00:08:45.093 --> 00:08:45.993
ever touching it.

00:08:46.833 --> 00:08:51.513
Semiconductor engineering's panel on scaling that test past one die treats fiber alignment

00:08:51.513 --> 00:08:53.573
as the bottleneck on the optical engine.

00:08:54.153 --> 00:08:57.913
The fiber array unit is meant to couple light and never contact the device.

00:08:58.653 --> 00:09:00.853
Crash it and bring up and the array is damaged.

00:09:00.853 --> 00:09:06.033
Leave contamination on it and the reading is useless, so cleaning sits inside the test cell.

00:09:06.513 --> 00:09:11.193
Dave Armstrong of ISC Labs, part of ASC Group, draws the power limit.

00:09:11.713 --> 00:09:17.493
An 8kW GPU with connectors on several sides asks the tester to push that power in and

00:09:17.493 --> 00:09:20.733
pull the heat out, and that is already hard past one die.

00:09:21.393 --> 00:09:26.753
Matt Griffin at TeraDine says most production cells today are single-site, and that multi-site

00:09:26.753 --> 00:09:29.833
probe cards would ease fiber alignment if they actually work.

00:09:29.833 --> 00:09:34.233
IRA 11thall at Advanced Test uses the ball grid array as the warning.

00:09:34.873 --> 00:09:37.653
Socket apart too many times and the balls are at risk.

00:09:38.193 --> 00:09:43.973
The optical connector on the device is built to be mated once and the hope is never unplugged.

00:09:44.413 --> 00:09:48.493
A test connector that survives 20-50 insertions is not a production tool.

00:09:48.973 --> 00:09:52.093
It needs tens of thousands of insertions or a hundred thousand.

00:09:52.673 --> 00:09:57.293
The panel's answer is hardened metal on the tester side, mating to a device receptacle

00:09:57.293 --> 00:10:02.013
that is not hardened, so a rough make can kill the device connector before it's spec life.

00:10:02.613 --> 00:10:07.573
Kazuo Yamaguchi at Keysight splits the easy contact from the one that qualifies the engine.

00:10:08.213 --> 00:10:14.573
DC pads plus an optical probe are mechanical. Modulator and photo detector proof is S parameters,

00:10:15.093 --> 00:10:18.833
so light and high frequency radio frequency probes have to land together.

00:10:19.533 --> 00:10:24.193
Probe cards carry only so many radio frequency lines, and their bandwidth is limited.

00:10:24.193 --> 00:10:29.853
While these devices are characterized past 200 gigahertz, Levinthal adds warpage.

00:10:30.273 --> 00:10:35.393
Alignment has to hold on several axes, from the top or the side, while a dense ball-grid

00:10:35.393 --> 00:10:36.693
array still has to connect.

00:10:37.413 --> 00:10:41.733
Griffin's package map puts an optical face and an electrical face on every insertion.

00:10:42.093 --> 00:10:47.633
Sometimes top, sometimes bottom, sometimes both, and at module level on two to four sides

00:10:47.633 --> 00:10:49.233
across several optical engines.

00:10:49.233 --> 00:10:54.453
options. Optical alignment alone, he says, is not the hard part, doing it on every face

00:10:54.453 --> 00:11:00.813
at once with power and radio frequency is. Walk Armstrong's Split, the 8kW GPU with

00:11:00.813 --> 00:11:05.813
connectors on several sides already strains one tester insertion, so a second sight buys

00:11:05.813 --> 00:11:11.333
nothing if the tester cannot feed it. Photonic integrated circuit way for test in his experience

00:11:11.333 --> 00:11:16.873
is single-site now, with a chance to rise if probe card makers and he names Technoprobe

00:11:16.873 --> 00:11:22.153
can put more optical sights on one card. Near-packaged optics is usually one

00:11:22.153 --> 00:11:27.413
connector. High volume of that class forces multi-site because one alignment per

00:11:27.413 --> 00:11:31.733
tester hour will not clear the line. He calls insertions two and three the

00:11:31.733 --> 00:11:36.773
fertile ground, the long insertions where multi-site can take time out. Single-site

00:11:36.773 --> 00:11:41.053
stays rational while that eight kilowatt-asix still exceeds what the tester can

00:11:41.053 --> 00:11:45.453
give a second die, while each site still needs its own clean fiber array that

00:11:45.453 --> 00:11:50.573
must not touch the die, and while the measurement that matters is an electrooptic S-parameter

00:11:50.573 --> 00:11:53.773
past 200 gigahertz that a probe card cannot fan out.

00:11:54.353 --> 00:11:58.653
It stops being the right cell when the product is a single connector near-packaged engine

00:11:58.653 --> 00:12:03.993
in high volume, insertions 2 and 3 on the test time, and a hardened test connector

00:12:03.993 --> 00:12:08.693
can survive on the order of 100,000 meetings without destroying the softer receptacle on

00:12:08.693 --> 00:12:09.053
the part.

00:12:09.053 --> 00:12:16.393
On the horizon, construction of fab-22 phase-4 in Kaohsiung is set to finish next year, on a site

00:12:16.393 --> 00:12:22.173
whose steel work is now stopped. Commercial production at the TSMC and Sony Image Sensor Venture in

00:12:22.173 --> 00:12:29.253
Kumamoto is scheduled for 2029. Amazon's Germany pledge, including data center expansion, is dated to

00:12:29.253 --> 00:12:38.194
2027, and Dell does not expect meaningful new memory fab supply until 2029 or 2030. Before we go,

00:12:38.194 --> 00:12:42.894
So watch whether labor inspectors in Kaohsiung assign liability for the snapped connecting

00:12:42.894 --> 00:12:43.574
plate bolts.

00:12:44.214 --> 00:12:46.334
That's AI Chips and Data Centers for today.

